    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it really comes down to whether the event was truly \"unforeseeable\" or just a known risk. If the disruption is caused by something that feels almost arbitrary or fundamentally disruptive to the normal order of things—not a specific named event, but just a sense of chaos that prevents operations—how does a lawyer frame that in an argument to ensure it isn't dismissed as \"speculative\"?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
