      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In such cases, lawyers might frame the disruption as an \"unprecedented event\" or a situation where the \"normal course of life\" was \"substantially disrupted\". This language can help argue that the event was unforeseeable at the time of contract formation, focusing on the fact that it was novel and unpredictable rather than simply speculative. Additionally, highlighting the unprecedented nature of the global pandemic or other recent events that may be cited as analogs can also help demonstrate that such unforeseen disruptions can have a legitimate impact on businesses.",
